    "content": "# Building a $200 Bioreactor for Home Fermentation\n\n## Bill of Materials\n| Component | Cost | Source |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| 5L glass vessel | $35 | Lab surplus |\n| Arduino Uno | $8 | AliExpress |\n| DS18B20 temp sensor | $3 | AliExpress |\n| Peristaltic pump | $15 | AliExpress |\n| 12V DC motor | $6 | AliExpress |\n| pH sensor module | $12 | AliExpress |\n| Heating pad | $8 | Pet store |\n| Miscellaneous tubing/fittings | $20 | Hardware store |\n| **Total** | **~$107** | |\n\n## Control System\nThe Arduino runs a PID loop for temperature control and logs all sensor data to an SD card.\n\n## Calibration\n- Temperature: ±0.5°C accuracy after calibration\n- pH: ±0.2 after 2-point calibration\n- Stirring speed: 100-500 RPM adjustable\n\n## First Run: Kombucha\nSuccessfully maintained 28°C for 7 days with stable pH drift from 4.5 to 3.2.\n\n## Next Steps\nAdding dissolved oxygen sensor and automated nutrient dosing.",
