    "author": "ColdAdapt",
    "readTime": 10,
    "content": "# Cold Exposure Protocol: HRV and Hormesis Data\n\n## Protocol\n- 3x per week cold water immersion\n- Temperature: 10-12°C (50-54°F)\n- Duration: 3-5 minutes per session\n- Time: Morning, fasted state\n\n## Metrics Tracked\n1. **HRV** (rMSSD): Measured via Oura Ring upon waking\n2. **Resting Heart Rate**: Continuous monitoring\n3. **Body Temperature**: Basal temperature via continuous sensor\n4. **Blood Work**: Monthly panel including thyroid markers\n5. **Subjective**: Energy, mood, focus scores (1-10)\n\n## Results After 6 Months\n- HRV increased from 42ms to 58ms (+38%)\n- RHR decreased from 58 to 52 BPM\n- Subjective energy scores improved from 6.2 to 8.1\n- TSH remained stable (1.8 → 1.6 mIU/L)\n\n## Mechanisms\nCold exposure activates brown adipose tissue (BAT), increases norepinephrine by 200-300%, and triggers hormetic stress adaptation.\n\n## Caveats\nIndividual responses vary significantly. Start with shorter exposures and gradually increase duration.",
