    "author": "PlasmidPunk",
    "readTime": 14,
    "content": "# Open Source Plasmid Design with Benchlingo\n\n## What is a Plasmid?\nA plasmid is a circular DNA molecule that can replicate independently of chromosomal DNA. They're the workhorses of molecular biology.\n\n## Design Workflow\n1. Define your goal (protein expression, gene knockout, reporter assay)\n2. Select backbone (pUC19, pET, pGEX, etc.)\n3. Add your insert using Gibson assembly or restriction cloning\n4. Verify with in silico digestion\n5. Order synthesized DNA from commercial providers\n\n## Free Tools\n- **Benchlingo**: Cloud-based molecular biology suite\n- **SnapGene Viewer**: Free plasmid visualization\n- **NEBcutter**: Restriction enzyme analysis\n- **Jit**: Codon optimization\n\n## Cost Breakdown\n- Gene synthesis (1kb): ~$50-100\n- Restriction enzymes: ~$30 each\n- Competent cells: ~$20/50 reactions\n- Agar plates: ~$0.50 each (homemade)\n\n## Verification\nAlways sequence your final construct. Sanger sequencing costs ~$5-8 per read and catches 95% of cloning errors.",
